WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.113 --> 00:00:01.530
JEN PERSON: Modern
businesses need

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:04.480
to manage not only the
identities of their employees,

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:07.000
but also the identities
of customers, partners,

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.220
and things.

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:11.460
Find out how to manage customers
in this episode of "Who's

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:12.762
There?"

00:00:12.762 --> 00:00:17.950
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:19.830
Welcome to "Who's
There," a show where

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:21.690
we explore Cloud Identity.

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:24.270
Today, I am talking
about the app management

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:28.650
facet of Cloud Identity, which
is called Identity Platform.

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:30.480
Identity Platform
lets you manage

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.210
the identities of customers,
partners, and things

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:35.070
through a single service.

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:37.920
It adds Google grade identity
and access management

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:41.130
functionality to your
apps and services.

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:44.760
With Identity Platform, you
can add a widely adopted, user

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:46.890
friendly, and customizable
authentication

00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:49.800
service to your web and
mobile apps with ease,

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:53.340
so you can focus on building
your app or service.

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:55.920
It supports multiple
authentication methods,

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:00.540
including SAML, OIDC,
email/password, social, phone,

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:03.480
and custom auth, to provide
flexible integration options

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:06.090
for any identity solution.

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:08.280
You can access Cloud
Identity through a range

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:11.920
of app SDKs for
Android, iOS, and web,

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:15.620
as well as server side Admin
SDKs for no Node.js, Java,

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:18.180
Python, and more.

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:20.670
To get your app up and
running even faster,

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:23.160
Identity Platform
provides a drop in,

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:25.950
customizable authentication
service for user sign

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:28.110
up and sign in.

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:30.510
When Google Cloud built
Identity Platform,

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:34.560
we wanted to meet the demands
of virtually any app or service.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:37.350
That's why it's built on
Google Cloud's global scale

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:39.870
performance network
and security.

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:43.710
And it comes with an enterprise
grade support and SLA.

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:46.680
You can secure user accounts
and scale with confidence

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:50.100
as it protects your app's users,
and prevents account takeovers

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:52.410
by integrating with Google's
intelligence for account

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:53.790
protection.

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:56.450
OK, I think I've spent
enough time telling you why

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:58.230
Identity Platform is awesome.

00:01:58.230 --> 00:02:02.250
Let's dive into how to configure
it for your Google project.

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:05.520
Before you get started, you need
to have a GCP project for which

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:07.440
you are a project
owner with billing

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:10.130
enabled for that project.

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:11.900
Once your project
is ready to go,

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:16.400
you can enable Identity Platform
from the GCP marketplace.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:18.440
Go to the Identity
Platform marketplace

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:21.230
page in the GCP console.

00:02:21.230 --> 00:02:24.650
Turn on Identity Platform
by clicking Enable Identity

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:25.550
Platform.

00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:28.970
Next, navigate to
the GCP console.

00:02:28.970 --> 00:02:32.810
You are now ready to start
using Identity Platform client

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:37.510
and Admin SDKs for
your apps and services.

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:39.700
After you enable
Identity Platform,

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:41.740
you can configure
authentication methods

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:45.540
so that your users can sign into
your applications and services.

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:47.680
I'll choose to
enable email/password

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:50.600
for this example.

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:53.810
Now you know how to get Identity
Platform up and running.

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:55.220
So what comes next?

00:02:55.220 --> 00:02:57.520
You can use Identity
Platform client SDKs

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:00.670
for Android, iOS, and
web to allow end users

00:03:00.670 --> 00:03:02.930
to authenticate your service.

00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:06.490
You can also use it server
side with the Admin SDK

00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:10.780
to migrate users or
customize user access level.

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:13.510
And there's a command line
option for migrating users

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:15.550
to Identity Platform.

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:17.410
To find out how to
complete these tasks

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:20.790
and more, check out the
documentation link below.

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:22.540
You can also check out
the Getting Started

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:24.670
videos for iOS,
Android, and web,

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:27.760
and then the Admin SDKs right
here on the Google Cloud

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:29.360
YouTube channel.

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:31.282
Thanks for watching
"Who's There."

00:03:31.282 --> 00:03:32.740
Be sure to subscribe
to the channel

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:35.530
to be the first to know about
new episodes of the series.

00:03:35.530 --> 00:03:39.480
